Hi all.  I'm struggling to install the new Rstan (see some details below).   I wonder if we could have some more automated instructions, maybe a makefile or whatever it is called?  Looking at the help file, it seems pretty algorithmic (if the computer has X installed, do Y, if it's a mac, do this, if it's a PC, do that, it if's later than version Z, do this, etc), so maybe that could all be put in a script?  As is, I'd say that of the 5 or so times I've installed Stan, it's worked the first time about half the time, other times I need to get help.  So, even though doing an automated install would be a pain in the ass, maybe it would not be so bad, as it would formalize all the choices in the install in one programmed place.  Then we can have a document for the experts explaining what got done.

