On Monday, February 10, 2014 1:53:59 PM UTC-5, Andrew Gelman wrote:
> Hi, Ben and Jiqiang.  I tried it in a regular R terminal and I got an error early on.  See the session which I've cut and pasted below.  It gives me an error with C++ which seems strange, given that I've run Stan in the past.
> The other thing that baffles me is that I just reinstalled R before following the instructions, but it still gave me this weird warning message at the beginning:
>
> Warning: namespace ‘rstan’ is not available and has been replaced
> by .GlobalEnv when processing object ‘fit’
> [Workspace restored from /Users/andrew/.RData]
> [History restored from /Users/andrew/.Rapp.history]

This may be part of the problem. The file that was saved when you closed a previous session, /Users/andrew/.RData , presumably contains an object of S4 class stanfit and thus when you start R, it tries to shallow load a copy of rstan, which doesn't exist because you uninstalled it. So, you could try moving or deleting /Users/andrew/.RData and /Users/andrew/.Rapp.history . However, I think you have other Mac-related problems below, that I don't know much about. But it looks like from

> > hellofun <- cxxfunction(body = src, includes = '', plugin = 'Rcpp', verbose = FALSE)
> cc1plus: error: unrecognized command line option "-stdlib=libstdc++"
> file183d05e714e2f.cpp:1: error: bad value (native  -O3 -Wall -pedantic -Wconversion) for -mtune= switch
> make: *** [file183d05e714e2f.o] Error 1

that maybe you have a typo in your Makevars file for the -mtune=typo switch.

Ben

