What’s wrong with all science all the time?  :-p
We can split up messages into strings and numbers and let
the interfaces deal with formatting if we’d like, or we handle
it internally.  Latter easier, former maybe more useful?

> This is another place where it seems like we want to allow the calling
> language (R, Python, etc.) do this in their own idiomatic way.  I could
> be convinced otherwise, because the doc maintenance and config logic is
> a nightmare here.

Let the interfaces create the configuration however they want,
so long as they can translate it into a proper Stan configuration
object.

That said, inconsistencies here will be pain on the users list when we
tell someone to “set the adaptation target to 0.99” and there are three
ways to do that depending on the interface.

> I'm still not sure how Michael manhandled the
> command interface and samplers into their new formats.

Pure force of will.  And lots of free time.

