It's not line ends, it's spaces before line end that got striped. I
already configured my editor to stop doing that.

>
> 2. As to style in doc, I would prefer not to capitalize anything
> other than proper names. So that'd be "negative binomial",
> not "Negative Binomial".
>
> Sorry for being so picky, but I want our doc to be consistent and it
> hurts my head thinking about all these different parameterizations.
> Suggestions welcome for how to name them and which are most useful.
I totally agree, I'll fix this.

>
> 3. In the LaTeX description, the name shold be camel case to match
> the distribution name in the Stan code. So that'd be
>
ok

NegBinomialLogLocInvDisp(...)

or whatever you go with.

- Bob

