Good point.

The PRNG functions are currently set up to only be accessible
in the generated quantities block.  But in that block, there's
no way to read in previous values --- the generated quantities
aren't accessible from the previous iteration.

I don't know how we'd do Gibbs in the parameter block because
the parameters are controlled on the outside, not set on the inside
of a model.

Anybody have any ideas?

- Bob

